WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:06.370
German Chancellor Angela Merkel appeared to
be more than happy to promote her agenda in

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.250
the crowded hall in Davos.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:15.400
"I think we should understand our national
interest in a way that we think about the

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:26.009
interests of others and from that create win-win
situations that are the precondition for multilateralism."

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:30.560
That was apparently aimed at politicians like
Donald Trump, who put the interests of their

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.840
own country first.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.950
Japan's Prime Minister Shinzo Abe also made
it clear in Davos he remains committed to

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.470
open markets.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.330
No growth without free trade.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:01:03.390
Abe focused above all on digitization and
borderless data traffic.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:08.439
The hustle and bustle in Davos is as international
as usual - but the atmosphere is more subdued.

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:11.799
Brexit, climate change, stronger nationalism.

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:15.799
Instead of the world improving, the future
seems increasingly uncertain.

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:20.340
The trade conflict between China and the USA
hasn't been resolved either.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.880
And China is pleading for a reprieve.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.119
"The U.S. and Chinese economies can't live
without each other.

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:29.119
That's already the reality.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:36.759
So, the conclusion is that the relationship
must be mutually beneficial and win-win.

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:43.149
Cooperation serves the interests of both sides,
while confrontation harms them.

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:46.889
This is a basic principle."

00:01:46.889 --> 00:01:48.619
Everything sounds reasonable.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:51.740
Improve the world, treat each other fairly.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:59.710
Everyone here agrees.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:03:18.969
But: the world

00:03:18.969 --> 00:04:42.750
outside

00:04:42.750 --> 00:05:52.190
of 
Davos looks different.

